      "procedure": "Procedure\nFOR THE CUPCAKES:\nPreheat oven to 175C. Line a muffin pan with paper liners.\nIn a medium bowl, whisk together flour, baking soda and salt.\nIn a large bowl, cream together the granulated sugar, brown sugar, and butter until light and fluffy. Beat in the eggs one at a time, then stir in the vanilla extract. Beat in the peanut butter until well combined.\nGradually beat in the dry ingredients until just combined. Stir in the milk chocolate chips.\nFill the prepared muffin cups 2/3 full. Bake for 20-25 minutes, or until  a toothpick inserted into the center comes out clean. Let cool completely in the pan before frosting.\nFOR THE FROSTING AND TOPPINGS:\nIn a large bowl, cream together the butter and powdered sugar until light and fluffy. Beat in the vanilla extract and milk until frosting reaches desired consistency.\nIn a small bowl, whisk together the peanut butter, powdered sugar, and milk until smooth.\nFrost the cooled cupcakes. Drizzle with peanut butter drizzle, and top with Nature’s Garden Milk Chocolate Pretzels."
